Technology Stack Summary
Ingest & Storage
Amazon Kinesis Data Streams: High-throughput data ingestion buffer
Amazon S3: Primary data lake with lifecycle policies
Amazon S3 Glacier Deep Archive: Long-term cold storage
Content Extraction
Tesseract OCR: Self-hosted on EC2/ECS for image-to-text
Whisper (OpenAI): Self-hosted on SageMaker for audio transcription
Apache Tika: Text extraction on Lambda/ECS
Embedding Generation
multilingual-e5-large or Mistral-7B: Self-hosted on SageMaker Endpoints
Amazon SageMaker: Model hosting and auto-scaling
EC2 GPU instances (g5.xlarge): Alternative hosting for custom setups
Vector Storage (3-Tier)
Hot Tier: Amazon OpenSearch with k-NN (HNSW algorithm)
Warm Tier: Milvus on EKS with DiskANN
Cold Tier: S3 + Parquet with IVF-PQ compression
Keyword Search
Amazon OpenSearch: BM25 inverted index for exact matching
Knowledge Graph
Amazon Neptune: Graph database for entity relationships
spaCy: Self-hosted NER on Lambda
Query Pipeline
Amazon API Gateway + WAF: Secure API endpoint
ECS Fargate: Stateless query orchestrator
Mistral-7B on SageMaker: Query expansion
ColBERT-v2 or MiniLM on SageMaker: Re-ranking
Metadata & Orchestration
Amazon DynamoDB: Fast metadata lookup (parent-child relationships)
AWS Lambda: Event-driven processing triggers
Amazon EKS: Container orchestration for Milvus
Monitoring & Compliance
Amazon CloudWatch: Logs, metrics, and alarms
AWS CloudTrail: Immutable audit logs
DynamoDB: Analyst feedback storage
Key Architecture Principles
1. Filter-Then-Rank Guarantee
The architecture enforces pre-query filtering at multiple levels:

Payload-indexed HNSW in OpenSearch (filters applied during vector search)
Segment routing in Milvus (partition by time/classification)
Selectivity estimation routes high-selectivity queries to exact search
2. C2S Compliance
No external APIs: All models are self-hosted
AWS-native services only: No Bedrock, no Datadog
Air-gapped operation: All processing stays within the security boundary
3. Scalability
Horizontal scaling: ECS Fargate, SageMaker auto-scaling
Tiered storage: Hot/warm/cold tiers optimize cost and performance
Distributed processing: Kinesis + Lambda for parallel processing
4. Mission-Specific Features
Temporal decay scoring: Prioritizes recent intelligence
Knowledge graph enrichment: Entity-based result expansion
Multilingual support: Cross-lingual semantic search
Acoustic embeddings: Audio similarity search (wav2vec 2.0)
This architecture provides a comprehensive, NSA-compliant solution that handles 1 trillion objects with sub-second query latency while maintaining strict security and compliance requirements.





